ived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-06-22T13:45:55Z","updated_at":"2026-06-29T13:06:35Z","closed_at":"2026-06-29T13:06:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Bug report\n\n## Current behavior\n\nBehavior change between 1.5.0 and 1.6.0 related to `disabled` and `invalid` state. In 1.5.0, the `invalid` state would be added to the Control **even** when the control was `disabled`. In 1.6.0, this changed, and when the control is `disabled`, an `invalid` state is ignored.\n\n### Related Change\n\nhttps://github.com/atomiks/base-ui/blob/e6dc73dfa253e0c11513e93e0ce36939f828351f/packages/react/src/field/root/FieldRoot.tsx#L111\n\nRelates to #4890\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThis _might_ be the intended behavior, I just wanted to double-check with the maintainers.\n\n## Reproducible example\n\n\n### Base UI 1.5.0\n\ndisplays `data-invalid` on a control when both `disabled` and `invalid` are set on the `Field.Root`.\n\n<img width=\"1469\" height=\"461\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75c7b113-fc3e-4c5f-b2c0-97c9e21e0383\" />\n\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/yogmuxar-9lbmyjxq?file=src%2FApp.tsx\n\n### Base UI 1.6.0\n\nIf a field is `disabled`, `data-invalid` is no longer present.\n\n<img width=\"1505\" height=\"570\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a19aa899-c46c-41df-a8dd-44ff2432381b\" />\n\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/yogmuxar-rpzzwdhj?file=src%2FApp.tsx\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.